## Service checks

```bash
curl -fsS http://<service>/health
curl -fsS http://<service>/ready
curl -fsS http://<service>/metrics
```

`/health` verifies process liveness. `/ready` controls traffic eligibility and must be extended when the service gains required databases, caches, message brokers, or other startup/runtime dependencies.

## Deployment

The application repository publishes an immutable image using the full Git SHA. Deployment is a GitOps change in `gitops-config`; the same image must be promoted through environments without rebuilding.

## Rollback

Revert desired state in Git to the previously verified immutable image reference, open the required pull request, and allow the GitOps reconciler to restore that state. Follow the platform rollback procedure for emergency runtime intervention.

