## Common failure modes

### Readiness fails

1. Inspect `/ready` response and application logs.
2. Confirm required dependencies are healthy and reachable.
3. Confirm configuration/secrets are present.
4. Keep the instance out of traffic until readiness is restored.

### Elevated HTTP errors

1. Confirm scope by route/status code in metrics and structured logs.
2. Check dependency and saturation signals.
3. Compare the deployed image SHA with the last known-good release.
4. Roll back desired state if the release is causal and mitigation is safer than a forward fix.

